cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PPI_PDB_Scraper or a dataset built with it, please cite it as below."
title: "PPI_PDB_Scraper: a reproducible pipeline for curated protein–protein interface datasets from the PDB"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Marcos"
    family-names: "Elizalde-Horcada"
    alias: marcos-bioinformatics
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcos-bioinformatics/PPI_PDB_Scraper"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow (Python and R) that turns a list of PDB IDs into a
  curated dataset of protein–protein interfaces for machine learning: PDBe
  PISA-lite interfaces, RCSB biological assemblies and metadata, crystallographic
  and structural quality control, a PRODIGY-cryst filter for small interfaces,
  MMseqs2 clustering by connected components, a test set with the classes of
  Park and Marcotte, cluster-aware train/validation splits with family weights,
  hard negatives checked against IntAct, and a homology-leakage audit.
keywords:
  - protein–protein interactions
  - Protein Data Bank
  - PISA
  - dataset curation
  - machine learning
  - data leakage
  - Snakemake
